        "subtype": "bot_message",
        "text": "*[Bug 19127] Sys.timezone() gives strange warning in non-UTF-8 encoding*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=19127>\n\n--- Comment #3 from Sebastian Meyer (<mailto:seb.meyer@fau.de|seb.meyer@fau.de>) ---\n(In reply to Michael (Gemini) Chirico from comment #2)\n&gt; The difference observed between Ubuntu 24.04 and openSUSE\n&gt; Tumbleweed is caused by distribution locale packaging \n\nThis is a red herring: Of course I made sure to install the lv_LV locale on\nboth systems before testing.\n\n&gt; and the specific day of the week tested:\n\nThis seems to be the crucial point. I tested openSUSE (systemd 261.2) and\nUbuntu (systemd 255) on different days of the week. `LC_TIME=lv_LV timedatectl`\ndid not fail on Ubuntu 24.04 last Friday but it does now on Thursday.\n\nThanks for clarifying the weekday dependency of the bug.",
        "username": "r-bugs notifier",
        "icons": {
            "emoji": ":robot_face:"
        },
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1786610568.160589",
        "bot_id": "B06769YJX9Q",
        "app_id": "A024R9PQM",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "B0mp",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "[Bug 19127] Sys.timezone() gives strange warning in non-UTF-8 encoding",
                                "style": {
                                    "bold": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=19127"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n\n--- Comment #3 from Sebastian Meyer ("
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "mailto:seb.meyer@fau.de",
                                "text": "seb.meyer@fau.de"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": ") ---\n(In reply to Michael (Gemini) Chirico from comment #2)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_quote",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "The difference observed between Ubuntu 24.04 and openSUSE\n Tumbleweed is caused by distribution locale packaging "
                            }
                        ],
                        "contains_padding": true
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n\nThis is a red herring: Of course I made sure to install the lv_LV locale on\nboth systems before testing.\n\n"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_quote",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "and the specific day of the week tested:"
                            }
                        ],
                        "contains_padding": true
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n\nThis seems to be the crucial point. I tested openSUSE (systemd 261.2) and\nUbuntu (systemd 255) on different days of the week. "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "LC_TIME=lv_LV timedatectl",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\ndid not fail on Ubuntu 24.04 last Friday but it does now on Thursday.\n\nThanks for clarifying the weekday dependency of the bug."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
