        "text": "*[Bug 19138] New: .Rbuildignore could treat .jj the same as .git, .hg, etc*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=19138>\n\n            Bug ID: 19138\n           Summary: .Rbuildignore could treat .jj the same as .git, .hg,\n                    etc\n           Product: R\n           Version: R-devel (trunk)\n          Hardware: All\n                OS: All\n            Status: NEW\n          Severity: minor\n          Priority: P5\n         Component: Installation\n          Assignee: <mailto:R-core@R-project.org|R-core@R-project.org>\n          Reporter: <mailto:michaelchirico4@gmail.com|michaelchirico4@gmail.com>\n\nCreated attachment 3785\n  --&gt; <https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/attachment.cgi?id=3785&amp;action=edit>\nIgnore .jj, and use R\"[]\" string to reduce regex escaping\n\nI am now a heavy user of `jj` (jujutsu): <https:\/\/github.com\/jj-vcs\/jj>\n\nI _personally_ perceive it mature enough (30K stars, 50 releases, complements\nthe new GitHub `stack` feature) to warrant the extra few characters in\n`.vc_dir_names`, but would understand the need to let this proposal simmer for\na while longer yet.\n\nOne thing which might be nice is to enable VCS to \"hide themselves\" as well --\n`jj` does so with `git` by adding `\/*` in `.jj\/.gitignore`, thereby hiding\nitself from `git` immediately upon `jj git init`. But that's a much bigger lift\n&amp; would require re-designing `.Rbuildignore` rules a bit.\n\nAnother consideration would be for `R CMD build` to _automatically_ exclude\n`.`-prefixed directories (besides the supported `.aspell`), _without_\ntriggering a `NOTE`.",
